From 9a8a9d0cc591920b6c312921f7dcb49a5d71de6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: baverrr <342259467+baverrr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:27:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] Record from the Echo's voice pipeline

On the Echo Show the VOICE_RECOGNITION capture pipeline beamforms but
applies no gain, so speech reached the wake word and Vosk about 20 dB
quieter than from VOICE_COMMUNICATION and "Hey Raven" never fired.
Measured with speech at the usual distance: loudest second -40.7 dB and
wake score 0.991 from VOICE_RECOGNITION, -21.4 dB and 0.998 from
VOICE_COMMUNICATION, which adds gain, noise reduction and echo
cancellation.

- Add MIC_SOURCE and use it for the wake word.
- Add MicSpeechService, Vosk's SpeechService with the source as above
  instead of its hardcoded VOICE_RECOGNITION, and use it for speech
  recognition.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
